svxconnect (0.1.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A microphone or speaker whose stream starts but never runs is detected
    and reopened, instead of transmitting silence (or playing nothing) until
    the program is restarted. When a reopen does not help, TX stops and the
    banner says so. A 0-frame transmission is never silent in the log again.
  * The client certificate is renewed: a certificate the reflector pushes at
    login or mid-session is validated and stored, an expired certificate or
    one the reflector refuses is replaced through a request with the same
    key, --enroll handles an expired certificate, and the banner warns
    before the certificate expires.
  * Disconnect, reconnect and PTT while connecting never block: the connect
    worker is abortable and the TCP connect and TLS handshake have timeouts.
  * The reason a connection dropped is kept (the reflector's MsgError, TLS
    close, reset or local error), and a control channel or UDP audio path
    that goes silent is noticed and re-established.
  * The log sink is thread-safe, the control FIFO must be private to the
    user, the status file is no longer fsync'd every second, UDP crypto can
    never reuse a GCM nonce, and an app that was never started no longer
    reads (or closes) stdin.
  * Beeps play when they are made; another station given our talkgroup
    while we are keyed un-keys us; miniaudio's own log is kept at debug.

 -- Joeri Van Dooren <ure@on6ure.be>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 01:10:14 +0200

svxconnect (0.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Beeps honour the output volume and mute: the roger beep played at full
    level through a muted output, because beeps are written below the jitter
    buffer, where the volume and mute actually live.

 -- Joeri Van Dooren <ure@on6ure.be>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 16:18:46 +0200

